WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.301
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.302
We're here with
Timothy Olyphant.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:04.371
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.471
You know I've said this
in the past,

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.572
I'm a huge fan of the show
"Justified,"

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:07.940
which had a wonderful run.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.376
And now you've just
finished shooting

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.512
a new limited series,
8 new episodes of the show.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:15.048
-Yeah.
-Raylan Givens is back.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.350
-Yeah.
-But even more exciting,

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.585
your daughter,
your youngest daughter,

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.422
has been cast in the show.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.823
-Can I just say the first thing
that went through my mind?

00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:26.526
"Is it more exciting?"

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.561
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.465
I mean...

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.801
I'm happy for her,
don't get me wrong,

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.670
but why is --

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:42.341
I'm still, underneath
this bull[bleep] exterior,

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.477
just a neurotic actor.
-Yeah, yeah. I'm sorry.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.980
-And all I heard there was,
somehow my kid coming back

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.648
was more exciting...
-Let me rephrase that.

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:54.220
Just a fraction as exciting
as you being back.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.623
It's barely news that
your daughter is in it.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.957
-My daughter is playing
my daughter

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:02.661
in the "Justified" revival.
-That's exciting, yeah.

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:05.665
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.801
-She's still a teenager, right?
-She's a teenager.

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.970
-So what's it like having
a teenage daughter on set?

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.206
-I don't recommend it.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.207
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:17.977
You know, here's the downside.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.446
She, uh...

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:26.285
Here's one of the things about
"Justified" in particular

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:30.089
is that over time, you've earned
a little bit of reputation

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:33.292
where perhaps people,
and just how you are,

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.527
the number on the call sheet,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.463
people can be a little bit
nervous around you

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.798
or feel intimidated,

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.401
and they're just very
careful around you.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:44.637
We hired the one person,
guaranteed,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.239
doesn't feel that way at all.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.640
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.743
In fact, she's not only
not nervous around me,

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.811
she's kind of over it.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.312
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:57.183
So it's such a strange thing to
be working with your daughter,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.920
and you're, like, gonna
give a note or a suggestion...

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.256
-'Cause it should be known,
you're also an EP on the show.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.657
You're a producer on the show.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.792
-That's what I kept
reminding her.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.861
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:10.263
'Cause she's like,
"Dad, no. Stop it.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.965
[ Laughter ]
Ugh!

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:14.433
God!

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.869
Just leave me alone."

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:18.271
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.374
I'm like, "I'm the star
of the [bleep]...

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.474
You can't..."

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:23.643
Do you know what it's like

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.711
to have to whisper
to your daughter,

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.414
like, "You can't
talk to me like that."

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.983
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.286
On the set of your own show?

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.321
It's terrible.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.923
-I was like, "Nobody
talks to me like that.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:39.626
This is like..." Yeah.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.260
It was really quite lovely.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.497
-It's a bummer that she's also
playing your daughter,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.832
which she does in real life.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.300
I know you're not
the same person,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.636
but she must feel like she knows
exactly how to do it.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:51.937
-Seth, that's me.
-Yeah, that's you?

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:53.506
You're Raylan Givens? You are?
-Pretty much.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.341
-Well, to quote Snoop Dogg...

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.443
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.211
-That's what I'm trying
to get across.

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:01.247
-Which you've begged us to do.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.849
-It was an incredible
experience.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.886
I have to say,
she was remarkable,

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.554
and it was a joy to
work with her.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:09.621
She worked very hard.

00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:10.823
She auditioned for it,

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.892
and I wasn't surprised
that they hired her.

00:03:13.892 --> 00:03:16.295
It was really special.
-That's very cool.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:18.264
I did hear she did
some on-set polling.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.465
What was the polling
she was doing?

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.733
-Oh, she did all that
bull[bleep]

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.834
where she would put, like --

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.969
she'd write, like,
"Favorite Olyphant"

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:25.771
on a big board

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:28.107
and put my name and her name.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.977
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.880
Look -- the crew's laughing!

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.382
I lost in a landslide.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.416
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:39.018
Like, a landslide.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.419
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.555
It was like,
one "Star Wars" geek

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.056
that voted for me.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.292
He's like, "Oh, I saw him
in 'The Mandalorian.'"

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.494
He was the only guy
who gave me a vote.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.396
It was terrible.
-Yeah.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.798
-No, she was terrible.
-Oh, I'm very sorry.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:55.668
I'm very sorry that your life
continues to be so rough.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.570
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.607
I really, I cannot wait
to see "Justified" coming back,

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.408
and I'm very excited
about "Amsterdam" as well.

00:04:03.408 --> 00:04:04.410
-That's very kind of you.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.744
I'm just thrilled to be here.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:07.045
It's great to see you.
-It's always great to see you.

00:04:07.045 --> 00:04:08.180
-I'm in town, by the way.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.582
-I know, you're here
for three months.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.283
-So we can...
-If anybody drops out,

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:12.452
you'll be here, right?

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.553
-That's what I'm saying.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, no.

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.789
It's coming across
loud and clear.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:17.957
You guys,
that's Timothy Olyphant!

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.225
-Thank you.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.561
-"Amsterdam" is in theaters
Friday, October 7th.

